    "result_text": "All 33 tests pass. The change is complete and the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `bulkSignupWarning` rule for `POST /api/owners`: **true when more than 80 owners have already been created on the request's registration day, otherwise false.** The flag is computed at creation, persisted on the owner, and returned on both the create response and subsequent `GET /api/owners/{id}` (matching how `namesakeCount` and other derived fields work).\n\nChanges:\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `Boolean bulkSignupWarning` field (`bulk_signup_warning` column) with getter/setter.\n- **`AssignBulkSignupWarning.java`** (new function) \u2014 counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals this owner's adjusted registration day and sets the flag when the count exceeds 80. Mirrors `CheckDailyLimit`/`AssignNamesakeCount`, sharing the same daily-accumulation path.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new step into the pipeline after `assignNamesakeCount`, before `save`, inside the write transaction (so it runs after the registration date is resolved and counts only already-persisted owners).\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `bulkSignupWarning` boolean (readOnly) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct auto-maps it by name.\n- **DB schemas** (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `bulk_signup_warning BOOLEAN` column.\n\n`Cp22Tests` (fresh create \u2192 `bulkSignupWarning` false) and all 33 tests pass.",
